{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793581165800,"sessionID":"ses_util_oc_kgc_r1_P1","part":{"partID":"prt_199c4ac22001z70OQUln7UWLgh","sessionID":"ses_util_oc_kgc_r1_P1","messageID":"msg_199c49ad0001Dug5oK2KiQbq1R","type":"tool","id":"call_a26aa4fa274647c3bd10969d1b2d8e17","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"/Users/quy.doan/Workspace/kg/target/release/kg --help","workdir":"/private/tmp/utility-corpus-2026-11-02/kg"},"output":"kg indexes a repository's symbols and call/inheritance edges into a local\nSQLite index. It is consultative only: no hooks, no daemon, no network,\nno writes outside .kg/.\n\nUsage: kg [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  build       Index the repository into .kg/index.db (full atomic replacement)\n  callers     Who calls this symbol\n  callees     What does this symbol call\n  path        Shortest call path between two symbols via resolved call edges. Resolved static edges only — dynamic dispatch may hide paths. A reverse question is the same query with swapped arguments\n  impact      Files that call into <file> (impact direction: callers of the file)\n  dead        Dead-code candidates: indexed symbols with zero inbound call edges. Candidates only — dynamic dispatch and entry points are not proven absent\n  unresolved  Per-file unresolved-callee counts (where kg could not resolve calls)\n  symbols     Symbols of one indexed file, ordered by line\n  search      Symbol-level search: bm25-ranked FTS5 over identifier tokens\n  clones      Duplicate-block candidates: normalized 5-line-window shingle matches\n  stats       Index totals: files, symbols, edges, parse errors, sizes\n  hotspots    Pain-ranking of files: cyclomatic + LOC + churn-90d + fix-density\n  report      Four-section architecture report (overview, map, hotspots, fan-in)\n  doctor      Inspect index health (integrity, versions, staleness, orphans)\n  usage       Summarize the usage journal: calls, errors, latency, empty/stale rates. --verify replays sampled payload pointers against current source\n  mcp         Run the MCP stdio server (newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0; Amendment 8)\n  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nOptions:\n      --root <ROOT>\n          Repository root (default: nearest git root ancestor of cwd). Global: valid before or after the subcommand\n\n      --no-journal\n          Disable the usage journal for this invocation (Amendment 6)\n\n  -h, --help\n          Print help (see a summary with '-h')\n\n  -V, --version\n          Print version\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"kg indexes a repository's symbols and call/inheritance edges into a local\nSQLite index. It is consultative only: no hooks, no daemon, no network,\nno writes outside .kg/.\n\nUsage: kg [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  build       Index the repository into .kg/index.db (full atomic replacement)\n  callers     Who calls this symbol\n  callees     What does this symbol call\n  path        Shortest call path between two symbols via resolved call edges. Resolved static edges only — dynamic dispatch may hide paths. A reverse question is the same query with swapped arguments\n  impact      Files that call into <file> (impact direction: callers of the file)\n  dead        Dead-code candidates: indexed symbols with zero inbound call edges. Candidates only — dynamic dispatch and entry points are not proven absent\n  unresolved  Per-file unresolved-callee counts (where kg could not resolve calls)\n  symbols     Symbols of one indexed file, ordered by line\n  search      Symbol-level search: bm25-ranked FTS5 over identifier tokens\n  clones      Duplicate-block candidates: normalized 5-line-window shingle matches\n  stats       Index totals: files, symbols, edges, parse errors, sizes\n  hotspots    Pain-ranking of files: cyclomatic + LOC + churn-90d + fix-density\n  report      Four-section architecture report (overview, map, hotspots, fan-in)\n  doctor      Inspect index health (integrity, versions, staleness, orphans)\n  usage       Summarize the usage journal: calls, errors, latency, empty/stale rates. --verify replays sampled payload pointers against current source\n  mcp         Run the MCP stdio server (newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0; Amendment 8)\n  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nOptions:\n      --root <ROOT>\n          Repository root (default: nearest git root ancestor of cwd). Global: valid before or after the subcommand\n\n      --no-journal\n          Disable the usage journal for this invocation (Amendment 6)\n\n  -h, --help\n          Print help (see a summary with '-h')\n\n  -V, --version\n          Print version\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false,"state":{"itemId":"fc_014db85f08c29a48016ae7e06d77708191b160ce903a52fe83"}},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"/Users/quy.doan/Workspace/kg/target/release/kg --help\",\"workdir\":\"/private/tmp/utility-corpus-2026-11-02/kg\"}"},"time":{"start":1793581165602,"end":1793581165800}}}}
